%U A401442 3612710157,11248628657,35109222705,109828774817,344283161035,1081321286765,3402333122077
%N A401442 Number of ordered rooted trees with n nodes such that no two sibling subtrees are isomorphic as unordered rooted trees.
%C A401442 It is instructive to look at the first term that differs from A032027, which is a(9)=253, compared to A032027(9)=255. That's because A032027(9) counts two trees with sibling subtrees (()(())) and ((())()), one for each order in which they may appear, whereas both are excluded from a(9) because the subtrees are isomorphic as unordered trees.
%C A401442 Number of brace strings of length 2n which, when interpreted as a set in brace notation with commas omitted, are well-formed and contain no redundant elements. For example, the 3 relevant brace strings of length 8 (corresponding to n=4) are "{{}{{}}}", "{{{}}{}}" and "{{{{}}}}". The first two are both readable as the set whose elements are {} and {{}} (i.e. von Neumann natural number 2), and the third is readable as the set whose sole element is {{{}}}. In conventional brace notation we place commas between elements, e.g. "{{},{{}}}" instead of "{{}{{}}}"; here we omit them.
%C A401442 Also, number of ordered rooted trees whose underlying unordered rooted trees have trivial automorphism group. - _Brendan McKay_, Oct 26 2026
%C A401442 If the set of trees counted by a(n) is partitioned into equivalence classes of trees counted by A004111(n), then from first nonzero value the number of classes with cardinality exactly k appear to be described by A087811(n-4), A001752(n-5), A000601(n-6) for k=2,4,6 respectively. (Note that A087811 has different offset from the others, otherwise would be n-3, alternatively use A002620(n-2)).
%H A401442 Adrian Morgan, <a href="/A401442/a401442.py.txt">Python program</a>, 2026.
%o A401442 (Python) # See Links.
%o A401442 (PARI) lista(nn) = my(ps=vector(nn)); forstep(j=nn, 1, -1, my(l=nn\j, e=1+O('x^l)); for(n=1, l, my(c=polcoef(e, n-1, 'x)); ps[j]+=sum(k=0, n-1, k!^j*polcoef(c, k, 'y))*'x^n; e*=exp(sum(i=1, (l-1)\n, (-1)^(i-1)*'y^i/i*polcoef(ps[i*j], n, 'x)*'x^(n*i))+O('x^l)))); Vecrev(ps[1]/'x); \\ _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 16 2026
%Y A401442 Cf. A004111 (unordered version).
%Y A401442 Cf. A032027 (version where sibling subtrees are different, as opposed to not isomorphic as unordered, identical for first 8 terms).
%K A401442 nonn,new
%O A401442 1,4
%A A401442 _Adrian Morgan_, Oct 25 2026
%E A401442 More terms from _Sean A. Irvine_, Nov 16 2026
